<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Adaptive-icon foreground: the Volleyball Lab mark itself.

  This replaced a drawn volleyball-seam vector. The mark is the app's identity
  everywhere else - splash, login, sign-up - and a launcher icon that shows
  something different is the one place the branding does not line up.

  ## Why 60 dp inside a 108 dp canvas

  Launchers guarantee only the centre 66 dp of the foreground survives their mask;
  everything outside can be clipped, and on a circular mask it will be. The mark is
  a circular badge, so it is placed at 60 dp - inside the safe zone with a little
  room to spare, rather than filling it edge to edge, which would leave a circular
  badge kissing the rim of a circular mask.

  ## Why the source is square

  `volleyball_lab_logo.png` is padded to 340x340. A layer-list item with a fixed
  width and height scales a bitmap to those bounds without preserving aspect ratio,
  so a 331x340 source would arrive 3% squashed - not obvious in isolation, and
  quite obvious next to the same mark drawn correctly on the splash.
-->
<layer-list xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android">
    <item
        android:width="60dp"
        android:height="60dp"
        android:drawable="@drawable/volleyball_lab_logo"
        android:gravity="center" />
</layer-list>
